pi-human-message is an independent community project and is not affiliated
with xAI, Telegram, or the Pi maintainers.

The evaluation-only reference prompts in scripts/prompt-variants.ts adapt ideas
from these MIT-licensed projects:

- Grok Telegram Bot contributors, grok-telegram-bot
  https://github.com/artickc/grok-telegram-bot
- Jack, learn-grok-bot
  https://github.com/yuanyijie/learn-grok-bot

Those reference prompts are used only as reproducible comparison baselines.
They are not claimed to be xAI's private production prompts.

The unreleased terminal chat-display design also draws on implementation
lessons from these MIT-licensed community projects:

- Kevin Vargas, pi-quiet-activity
  https://github.com/kevinvargasl/pi-quiet-activity/tree/51fc7979df7b2e7df044a1ce4cd90701c4cb6347
- leblancfg, pi-quiet-tools
  https://github.com/leblancfg/pi-quiet-tools/tree/a0fbdffabbbcdaa610d77b80ade305f0b6f9ab6a

These are design references, not copied source code or upstream endorsements.
In particular, display filtering stays separate from tool execution, and
compatibility failures preserve the original view.
